.TH PVE\-CEPH\-UPGRADE 8 "2026-06-17" "1.0.1" "Proxmox VE Tools"
.SH NAME
pve\-ceph\-upgrade \- online Ceph major\-release migration for a Proxmox VE hyper\-converged cluster
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pve\-ceph\-upgrade
.B \-\-to
.I release
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B pve\-ceph\-upgrade
.B \-\-to
.I release
.RB [ \-\-from
.IR release ]
.RB [ \-\-jump
.IR user @ host ]
.RB [ \-\-stable
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pve\-ceph\-upgrade
migrates the Ceph cluster embedded in a Proxmox VE hyper\-converged cluster from
one major release to the next (for example
.I squid
to
.IR tentacle ),
.B online
and with no guest downtime. It stages the new packages on every node, then
restarts the daemons in the order the upstream procedure mandates \(em
.BR monitor " \(-> " manager " \(-> " OSD " \(-> " MDS
\(em gating on Ceph health and quorum between every step, and only flips
.B require\-osd\-release
once every OSD reports the new release.
.PP
This is the Ceph\-major counterpart to
.BR pve\-rolling\-upgrade (8):
that tool performs the PVE 8\(->9 distribution jump and deliberately leaves Ceph
on its current major; this tool performs the Ceph major and touches nothing
about the Debian/PVE release. Run them as
.B separate passes
\(em never combine a Ceph major with a distribution upgrade.
.PP
Topology (cluster nodes, monitor/manager/OSD/MDS placement, CephFS name and its
standby\-replay setting, source release) is
.B auto\-discovered
from the live cluster.
.SH SAFETY
.B This is a production, hard\-to\-reverse operation.
A Ceph major upgrade is one\-way once
.B require\-osd\-release
is set. Always read the version\-specific upstream notes first \(em
.I https://pve.proxmox.com/wiki/Ceph_<From>_to_<To>
\(em as the exact daemon order and any pre\-steps are release\-specific. The
cluster must already be fully on PVE 9 (Trixie), HEALTH_OK (bar a
.I noout
warning), with every daemon on the source release, all PGs
.IR active+clean ,
and quorate.
.B \-\-dry\-run
performs read\-only discovery and prints the plan. The tool
.B hard\-stops
(non\-zero exit) on any failed gate.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-to " " \fIrelease\fR
Target Ceph release, e.g.
.IR tentacle .
.B Required.
.TP
.BR \-\-from " " \fIrelease\fR
Source release. Default: auto\-detect from
.BR "ceph versions" .
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jump " " \fIuser\fR@\fIhost\fR
ProxyJump/bastion host used to reach the cluster.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stable " " \fIhost\fR
A monitor node used to drive cluster\-wide Ceph and quorum checks. Required when
the cluster cannot otherwise be reached.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Proceed without the interactive confirmation (required for unattended runs).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Discover and print the plan without changing anything.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colour (also disabled automatically when stdout is not a TTY).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
OK \(em every daemon migrated to the target release and health is OK.
.TP
.B 1
FAIL \(em a pre\-condition or gate failed and the run halted; inspect Ceph.
.TP
.B 2
USAGE \(em bad invocation, a missing dependency, or the cluster was unreachable.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Overrides may be set in the environment or in
.IR /etc/pve\-ceph\-upgrade.conf
(a sourced shell file).
.TP
.B PVE_CU_SSH_OPTS
Extra
.BR ssh (1)
options (ProxyJump, IdentityFile, ...).
.TP
.B PVE_CU_JUMP
Convenience ProxyJump host (same as
.BR \-\-jump ).
.TP
.B PVE_CU_REPO_BASE
Override the Ceph repository (base URL and component). Default:
.I http://download.proxmox.com/debian/ceph\-<to>
with the
.I no\-subscription
component.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Preview a Squid\(->Tentacle migration through a bastion (no changes):
.PP
.RS
.EX
pve\-ceph\-upgrade \-\-dry\-run \-\-to tentacle \-j root@bastion \-s pve01
.EE
.RE
.PP
Perform the migration (asks to confirm first):
.PP
.RS
.EX
pve\-ceph\-upgrade \-\-to tentacle \-j root@bastion \-s pve01
.EE
.RE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Controller:
.BR bash ", " ssh ", " curl .
Each node: the Ceph/PVE stack
.RB ( ceph ", " systemctl ", " apt ).
Node names from
.BR "pvecm nodes"
must be reachable from the controller (directly or through
.BR \-\-jump ).
Key\-based root SSH is assumed.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR pve\-rolling\-upgrade (8),
.BR pve\-sdn\-healthcheck (8),
.BR ceph (8)
.PP
Upstream procedure:
.I https://pve.proxmox.com/wiki/Ceph_Squid_to_Tentacle
